nightlightd is a zero-config screen colour temperature daemon for X11,
a modern alternative to redshift and gammastep. It reads the timezone
to find the sun, re-applies the gamma ramp after suspend, resolution
change or monitor hotplug, and refuses to run twice.

Programs:
  nightlightd       daemon and CLI (nightlightd --daemon, --status)
  nightlight-tray   tray icon
  nightlight-panel  settings window (desktop menu entry)
  nightlight-tui    terminal dashboard

Build dependencies:
  - rust / cargo (edition 2024: Rust 1.85 or newer)
  - network access for crates.io at build time
Runtime dependencies for nightlight-panel (all in stock Slackware):
  libX11, libXrandr, libXcursor, libXi, libxkbcommon, Mesa (GL).

Options:
  PANEL=no           skip nightlight-panel (slowest part of the build)
  CARGO_BUILD_FLAGS  extra flags passed to cargo build

Autostart:
  The package installs XDG autostart entries in /etc/xdg/autostart for
  the daemon and the tray icon. Remove the .desktop files, or copy
  them to ~/.config/autostart with Hidden=true, to disable them.
  Slackware has no systemd; a user unit is still installed in
  /usr/lib/systemd/user for systemd users.
